# Friendica core is FETCHED, never committed.
#
# Three reasons this matters, and they are not style preferences:
#   * core is upstream's tree, not ours — the only thing we want to know about it is "does it
#     still match upstream", which is a question you can only ask of a real checkout;
#   * committing it would make every upstream release a merge of thousands of files we do not
#     own, instead of a fast-forward;
#   * it is what lets tools/dev/check-core-clean.sh be a meaningful check rather than a
#     comparison of our tree against itself.
/friendica/

# Local runtime state: the project-local MariaDB datadir, server logs, pid files, and the
# generated configuration of any instance provisioned by tools/dev/instance.sh.
/.local/

# The installer's answers hold passwords - the example template is committed, real ones never are.
packaging/.env

# Release zips are built artifacts (packaging/make-dist.sh), not sources.
/dist/

# Tool state, not project code.
/.freebuff/

# Python bytecode, e.g. from compiling the end-to-end suite to check it before running it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor and OS noise.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
